From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:23:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: samsung: Add the Galaxy S10 audio driver

Tie the two speaker amplifiers to UAIF1 of the ABOX: I2S with the SoC
providing both clocks, the amplifier PLLs referenced to the bit clock,
and each amplifier on the channel its position in the codec list gives.
The earpiece takes the left channel and the bottom speaker the right
one, which the voltage and current monitors of both amplifiers confirm:
a 1 kHz tone on the left channel and a 500 Hz tone on the right come back
from the earpiece and the bottom speaker respectively, with no trace of
the other tone.

ASPTX2 of both amplifiers comes out of reset fed by IMON and placed in
slot 1. With two slots on the port that puts three transmitters on the
shared SDOUT line as soon as the port records, which shows up as a slot
full of zeros and half values. The card sets the ASPTX2 source mux to
Zero, which leaves the channel unpowered. That has to go through the mux
control, since DAPM keeps the path it read from the register when the
routes went in, and the control only exists once the card is bound, so
it is done right after the card is registered.

The CS47L93 codec is the second link, on UAIF0 with the codec as the
clock consumer. The 26 MHz MCLK1 the vendor feeds the codec comes from
the PMU clock output, which has no driver, so FLL1 locks to the bit
clock of the port instead and SYSCLK runs at 98.304 MHz from it. ABOX
starts the bit clock when a stream is prepared, before DAPM powers the
codec, so the card starts FLL1 on the way into the prepare bias level of
the codec and stops it on the way out. With a 1 kHz tone on the earpiece
and 500 Hz on the bottom speaker, the microphone on IN3 records the
bottom speaker (500 Hz at 36.1 against 1.4 at 1 kHz) and the one on IN4
the earpiece (1 kHz at 23.6 against 1.3 at 500 Hz).

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 MAINTAINERS                      |   1 +
 sound/soc/samsung/Kconfig        |  14 ++
 sound/soc/samsung/Makefile       |   2 +
 sound/soc/samsung/beyond-audio.c | 339 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 356 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/samsung/beyond-audio.c

